# Security principles

Read **`principles/security.md`** in the ai-skills repo before writing or reviewing code.

- Validate external input; never use raw user input in sensitive operations.
- Do not expose secrets in code, logs, or public artifacts.
- Fail securely; ship secure-by-default configurations.
- Keep designs simple to reduce attack surface.

When an employer- or domain-specific security rule pack is open in the workspace, follow it in addition to `principles/security.md`. Convention: a repo named **`{domain}-cursor-rules`** (e.g. `uvcyber-cursor-rules`). If several are present, apply rules from repos that match the project you are editing.
